ss that cannot be delayed i have not an instant to lose'),(4766,1,676,46460,'good god'),(4767,1,994,6358,'what is the matter'),(4768,1,4916,636,'cried he with more feeling than politeness then recollecting himself i will not detain you a minute but let me or let the servant go after mr'),(4769,1,1,273,'and mrs'),(4770,1,2074,7312,'you are not well enough you cannot go yourself'),(4771,1,2133,112,'elizabeth hesitated but her knees trembled under her and she felt how little would be gained by her attempting to pursue them'),(4772,1,13254,12091,'calling back the servant therefore she commissioned him though in so breathless an accent as made her almost unintelligible to fetch his master and mistress home instantly'),(4773,1,407,43146,'on his quitting the room she sat down unable to support herself and looking so miserably ill that it was impossible for darcy to leave her or to refrain from saying in a tone of gentleness and commiseration let me call your maid'),(4774,1,75,16441,'is there nothing you could take to give you present relief'),(4775,1,23,139,'a glass of wine shall i get you one'),(4776,1,2074,5886,'you are very ill'),(4777,1,655,1755,'no i thank you she replied endeavouring to recover herself'),(4778,1,74,424,'there is nothing the matter with me'),(4779,1,279,7709,'i am quite well i am only distressed by some dreadful news which i have just received from longbourn'),(4780,1,729,1426,'she burst into tears as she alluded to it and for a few minutes could not speak another word'),(4781,1,2154,8550,'darcy in wretched suspense could only say something indistinctly of his illustration i have not an instant to lose concern and observe her in compassionate silence'),(4782,1,308,3373,'at length she spoke again'),(4783,1,279,5637,'i have just had a letter from jane with such dreadful news'),(4784,1,67,8412,'it cannot be concealed from anyone'),(4785,1,413,636,'my youngest sister has left all her friends--has eloped has thrown herself into the power of--of mr'),(4786,