elizabeth soon observed and instantly understood it'),(4814,1,382,29556,'her power was sinking everything must sink under such a proof of family weakness such an assurance of the deepest disgrace'),(4815,1,729,32212,'she could neither wonder nor condemn but the belief of his self-conquest brought nothing consolatory to her bosom afforded no palliation of her distress'),(4816,1,67,10080,'it was on the contrary exactly calculated to make her understand her own wishes and never had she so honestly felt that she could have loved him as now when all love must be vain'),(4817,1,295,382,'but self though it would intrude could not engross her'),(4818,1,90771,14482,'lydia--the humiliation the misery she was bringing on them all--soon swallowed up every private care and covering her face with her handkerchief elizabeth was soon lost to everything else and after a pause of several minutes was only recalled to a sense of her situation by the voice of her companion who in a manner which though it spoke compassion spoke likewise restraint said-- i am afraid you have been long desiring my absence nor have i anything to plead in excuse of my stay but real though unavailing concern'),(4819,1,126,32212,'would to heaven that anything could be either said or done on my part that might offer consolation to such distress'),(4820,1,295,8329,'but i will not torment you with vain wishes which may seem purposely to ask for your thanks'),(4821,1,37,13310,'this unfortunate affair will i fear prevent my sisters having the pleasure of seeing you at pemberley to-day'),(4822,1,5037,9487,'oh yes'),(4823,1,104,2154,'be so kind as to apologize for us to miss darcy'),(4824,1,794,5002,'say that urgent business calls us home immediately'),(4825,1,10628,346,'conceal the unhappy truth as long as it is possible'),(4826,1,279,2583,'i know it cannot be long'),(4827,1,258,4025,'he readily assured her of his secrecy again expressed his sorrow for her distress wished it a happier conclusion than there was at pr