ic lamp'),(7220,2,1502,129924,'then i had what i can only regard as an inspiration'),(7221,2,42,128875,'as a pressman i felt sure from what i had been told that i could never hope to get into touch with this cantankerous professor'),(7222,2,295,11882,'but these recriminations twice mentioned in his skeleton biography could only mean that he was a fanatic in science'),(7223,2,473,129981,'was there not an exposed margin there upon which he might be accessible'),(7224,2,279,46472,'i would try'),(7225,2,279,129857,'i entered the club'),(7226,2,67,50,'it was just after eleven and the big room was fairly full though the rush had not yet set in'),(7227,2,279,2140,'i noticed a tall thin angular man seated in an arm-chair by the fire'),(7228,2,258,247,'he turned as i drew my chair up to him'),(7229,2,67,1990,'it was the man of all others whom i should have chosen--tarp henry of the staff of nature a thin dry leathery creature who was full to those who knew him of kindly humanity'),(7230,2,279,1118,'i plunged instantly into my subject'),(7231,2,994,128876,'what do you know of professor challenger'),(7232,2,258,130086,'he gathered his brows in scientific disapproval'),(7233,2,128876,129699,'challenger was the man who came with some cock-and-bull story from south america'),(7234,2,994,582,'what story'),(7235,2,5037,7055,'oh it was rank nonsense about some queer animals he had discovered'),(7236,2,279,5543,'i believe he has retracted since'),(7237,2,95861,172,'anyhow he has suppressed it all'),(7238,2,258,513,'he gave an interview to reuter\'s and there was such a howl that he saw it wouldn\'t do'),(7239,2,67,661,'it was a discreditable business'),(7240,2,74,891,'there were one or two folk who were inclined to take him seriously but he soon choked them off'),(7241,2,43,130175,'well by his insufferable rudeness and impossible behavior'),(7242,2,74,130184,'there was poor old wadley of the zoological institute'),(7243,2,130180,3448,'wadley sent a message \'the president of the zool