iate with your profession'),(7611,2,50,11273,'in admitting that the fault of the incident lay with you you gave some evidence of a certain mental detachment and breadth of view which attracted my favorable notice'),(7612,2,51,134385,'the sub-species of the human race to which you unfortunately belong has always been below my mental horizon'),(7613,2,1373,67,'your words brought you suddenly above it'),(7614,2,2074,11273,'you swam up into my serious notice'),(7615,2,284,5984,'for this reason i asked you to return with me as i was minded to make your further acquaintance'),(7616,2,2074,134439,'you will kindly deposit your ash in the small japanese tray on the bamboo table which stands at your left elbow'),(7617,2,172,30341,'all this he boomed forth like a professor addressing his class'),(7618,2,258,134483,'he had swung round his revolving chair so as to face me and he sat all puffed out like an enormous bull-frog his head laid back and his eyes half-covered by supercilious lids'),(7619,2,2530,18039,'now he suddenly turned himself sideways and all i could see of him was tangled hair with a red protruding ear'),(7620,2,258,130797,'he was scratching about among the litter of papers upon his desk'),(7621,2,258,410,'he faced me presently with what looked like a very tattered sketch-book in his hand'),(7622,2,279,258,'i am going to talk to you about south america said he'),(7623,2,655,8565,'no comments if you please'),(7624,2,183,26343,'first of all i wish you to understand that nothing i tell you now is to be repeated in any public way unless you have my express permission'),(7625,2,163,747,'that permission will in all human probability never be given'),(7626,2,75,11120,'is that clear'),(7627,2,67,279,'it is very hard said i'),(7628,2,5320,8843,'surely a judicious account---- he replaced the notebook upon the table'),(7629,2,163,258,'that ends it said he'),(7630,2,279,6169,'i wish you a very good morning'),(7631,2,655,655,'no no'),(7632,2,279,4916,'i cried'),(7633,2,279,34