 on the chest finally pushing me back into my chair'),(8308,2,172,258,'all right sonny my lad--you\'ll do said he'),(8309,2,279,8294,'i looked up in surprise'),(8310,2,279,144573,'i saw after jack ballinger myself this mornin\''),(8311,2,258,5027,'he blew a hole in the skirt of my kimono bless his shaky old hand but we got a jacket on him and he\'s to be all right in a week'),(8312,2,279,144613,'i say young fellah i hope you don\'t mind--what'),(8313,2,2074,407,'you see between you an\' me close-tiled i look on this south american business as a mighty serious thing and if i have a pal with me i want a man i can bank on'),(8314,2,1051,67,'so i sized you down and i\'m bound to say that you came well out of it'),(8315,2,2074,183,'you see it\'s all up to you and me for this old summerlee man will want dry-nursin\' from the first'),(8316,2,3,144705,'by the way are you by any chance the malone who is expected to get his rugby cap for ireland'),(8317,2,23,290,'a reserve perhaps'),(8318,2,279,11135,'i thought i remembered your face'),(8319,2,4949,27658,'why i was there when you got that try against richmond--as fine a swervin\' run as i saw the whole season'),(8320,2,279,1811,'i never miss a rugby match if i can help it for it is the manliest game we have left'),(8321,2,43,46210,'well i didn\'t ask you in here just to talk sport'),(8322,2,143977,661,'we\'ve got to fix our business'),(8323,2,454,1061,'here are the sailin\'s on the first page of the times'),(8324,2,129216,144807,'there\'s a booth boat for para next wednesday week and if the professor and you can work it i think we should take it--what'),(8325,2,56,247,'very good i\'ll fix it with him'),(8326,2,994,144818,'what about your outfit'),(8327,2,413,163,'my paper will see to that'),(8328,2,850,108123,'can you shoot'),(8329,2,482,137750,'about average territorial standard'),(8330,2,676,22823,'good lord'),(8331,2,42,163,'as bad as that'),(8332,2,127528,144847,'it\'s the last thing you young fellahs think of learnin\'')