18,'declared it myself waged it myself ended it myself'),(8354,2,2163,145170,'each of those nicks is for a slave murderer--a good row of them--what'),(8355,2,163,4669,'that big one is for pedro lopez the king of them all that i killed in a backwater of the putomayo river'),(8356,2,2530,2074,'now here\'s something that would do for you'),(8357,2,258,145081,'he took out a beautiful brown-and-silver rifle'),(8358,2,43,145219,'well rubbered at the stock sharply sighted five cartridges to the clip'),(8359,2,2074,163,'you can trust your life to that'),(8360,2,258,128930,'he handed it to me and closed the door of his oak cabinet'),(8361,2,3,128876,'by the way he continued coming back to his chair what do you know of this professor challenger'),(8362,2,279,13310,'i never saw him till to-day'),(8363,2,43,279,'well neither did i'),(8364,2,127528,515,'it\'s funny we should both sail under sealed orders from a man we don\'t know'),(8365,2,258,137407,'he seemed an uppish old bird'),(8366,2,892,3279,'his brothers of science don\'t seem too fond of him either'),(8367,2,1338,4696,'how came you to take an interest in the affair'),(8368,2,279,40982,'i told him shortly my experiences of the morning and he listened intently'),(8369,2,1502,8843,'then he drew out a map of south america and laid it on the table'),(8370,2,279,163,'i believe every single word he said to you was the truth said he earnestly and mind you i have something to go on when i speak like that'),(8371,2,102297,140997,'south america is a place i love and i think if you take it right through from darien to fuego it\'s the grandest richest most wonderful bit of earth upon this planet'),(8372,2,7105,16809,'people don\'t know it yet and don\'t realize what it may become'),(8373,2,127793,145444,'i\'ve been up an\' down it from end to end and had two dry seasons in those very parts as i told you when i spoke of the war i made on the slave-dealers'),(8374,2,43,674,'well when i was up there i heard some yarns of the same kind-