6,'behind me the thick gasping breathing of the creature sounded louder and louder'),(10016,2,892,424,'his heavy footfall was beside me'),(10017,2,138,1886,'every instant i expected to feel his grip upon my back'),(10018,2,1,2096,'and then suddenly there came a crash--i was falling through space and everything beyond was darkness and rest'),(10019,2,42,176973,'as i emerged from my unconsciousness--which could not i think have lasted more than a few minutes--i was aware of a most dreadful and penetrating smell'),(10020,2,2748,135299,'putting out my hand in the darkness i came upon something which felt like a huge lump of meat while my other hand closed upon a large bone'),(10021,2,1274,818,'up above me there was a circle of starlit sky which showed me that i was lying at the bottom of a deep pit'),(10022,2,18229,554,'slowly i staggered to my feet and felt myself all over'),(10023,2,279,177060,'i was stiff and sore from head to foot but there was no limb which would not move no joint which would not bend'),(10024,2,42,135772,'as the circumstances of my fall came back into my confused brain i looked up in terror expecting to see that dreadful head silhouetted against the paling sky'),(10025,2,74,203,'there was no sign of the monster however nor could i hear any sound from above'),(10026,2,279,177132,'i began to walk slowly round therefore feeling in every direction to find out what this strange place could be into which i had been so opportunely precipitated'),(10027,2,67,26307,'it was as i have said a pit with sharply-sloping walls and a level bottom about twenty feet across'),(10028,2,37,177170,'this bottom was littered with great gobbets of flesh most of which was in the last state of putridity'),(10029,2,51,90605,'the atmosphere was poisonous and horrible'),(10030,2,171,143803,'after tripping and stumbling over these lumps of decay i came suddenly against something hard and i found that an upright post was firmly fixed in the center of the hollow'),(10031,2,67,177231,'it was so high that i could not reach the top of it with my hand and it appeared to be covered with grease'),(10032,2,5725,98513,'suddenly i remembered that i had a tin box of wax-vestas in my pocket'),(10033,2,32769,24022,'striking one of them i was able at last to form some opinion of this place into which i had fallen'),(10034,2,74,1212,'there could be no question as to its nature'),(10035,2,67,1278,'it was a trap--made by the hand of man'),(10036,2,51,67,'the post in the center some nine feet long was sharpened at the upper end and was black with the stale blood of the creatures who had been impaled upon it'),(10037,2,51,50,'the remains scattered about were fragments of the victims which had been cut away in order to clear the stake for the next who might blunder in'),(10038,2,279,67,'i remembered that challenger had declared that man could not exist upon the plateau since with his feeble weapons he could not hold his own against the monsters who roamed over it'),(10039,2,295,3873,'but now it was clear enough how it could be done'),(10040,2,50,13954,'in their narrow-mouthed caves the natives whoever they might be had refuges into which the huge saurians could not penetrate while with their developed brains they were capable of setting such traps covered with branches across the paths which marked the run of the animals as would destroy them in spite of all their strength and activity'),(10041,2,1278,22259,'man was always the master'),(10042,2,51,424,'the sloping wall of the pit was not difficult for an active man to climb but i hesitated long before i trusted myself within reach of the dreadful creature which had so nearly destroyed me'),(10043,2,1338,177501,'how did i know that he was not lurking in the nearest clump of bushes waiting for my reappearance'),(10044,2,279,135605,'i took heart however as i recalled a conversation between challenger and summerlee upon the habits of the great saurians'),(10045,2,1191,3413,'both were agreed that the monsters were 