aist cloth for flint and steel and stooped down to singe shere khans whiskers'),(12725,3,387,112,'most native hunters always singe a tigers whiskers to prevent his ghost from haunting them'),(12726,3,2257,212946,'said mowgli half to himself as he ripped back the skin of a forepaw'),(12727,3,1051,126913,'so thou wilt take the hide to khanhiwara for the reward and perhaps give me one rupee'),(12728,3,2530,1674,'now it is in my mind that i need the skin for my own use'),(12729,3,2018,2140,'old man take away that fire'),(12730,3,994,7711,'what talk is this to the chief hunter of the village'),(12731,3,202804,103880,'thy luck and the stupidity of thy buffaloes have helped thee to this kill'),(12732,3,51,369,'the tiger has just fed or he would have gone twenty miles by this time'),(12733,3,202806,171976,'thou canst not even skin him properly little beggar brat and forsooth i buldeo must be told not to singe his whiskers'),(12734,3,204077,174925,'mowgli i will not give thee one anna of the reward but only a very big beating'),(12735,3,4616,223765,'leave the carcass'),(12736,3,3,52181,'by the bull that bought me said mowgli who was trying to get at the shoulder must i stay babbling to an old ape all noon'),(12737,3,454,424,'here akela this man plagues me'),(12738,3,220532,128504,'buldeo who was still stooping over shere khans head found himself sprawling on the grass with a gray wolf standing over him while mowgli went on skinning as though he were alone in all india'),(12739,3,223833,88510,'ye-es he said between his teeth'),(12740,3,202806,220532,'thou art altogether right buldeo'),(12741,3,202806,128162,'thou wilt never give me one anna of the reward'),(12742,3,74,30484,'there is an old war between this lame tiger and myself--a very old war and--i have won'),(12743,3,40,17957,'to do buldeo justice if he had been ten years younger he would have taken his chance with akela had he met the wolf in the woods but a wolf who obeyed the orders of this boy who had private wars with man-eating tigers was not a common animal'),(12744,3,67,247,'it was sorcery magic of the worst kind thought buldeo and he wondered whether the amulet round his neck would protect him'),(12745,3,258,813,'he lay as still as still expecting every minute to see mowgli turn into a tiger too'),(12746,3,1108,15065,'great king he said at last in a husky whisper'),(12747,3,9487,262,'yes said mowgli without turning his head chuckling a little'),(12748,3,279,1278,'i am an old man'),(12749,3,279,223995,'i did not know that thou wast anything more than a herdsboy'),(12750,3,465,5872,'may i rise up and go away or will thy servant tear me to pieces'),(12751,3,351,203807,'go and peace go with thee'),(12752,3,241,15748,'only another time do not meddle with my game'),(12753,3,2792,204273,'let him go akela'),(12754,3,220532,130739,'buldeo hobbled away to the village as fast as he could looking back over his shoulder in case mowgli should change into something terrible'),(12755,3,483,12132,'when he got to the village he told a tale of magic and enchantment and sorcery that made the priest look very grave'),(12756,3,204077,133885,'mowgli went on with his work but it was nearly twilight before he and the wolves had drawn the great gay skin clear of the body'),(12757,3,2530,8866,'now we must hide this and take the buffaloes home'),(12758,3,4236,204273,'help me to herd them akela'),(12759,3,51,224148,'the herd rounded up in the misty twilight and when they got near the village mowgli saw lights and heard the conches and bells in the temple blowing and banging'),(12760,3,2361,53115,'half the village seemed to be waiting for him by the gate'),(12761,3,163,852,'that is because i have killed shere khan he said to himself'),(12762,3,295,224186,'but a shower of stones whistled about his ears and the villagers shouted sorcerer'),(12763,3,203327,220880,'wolfs brat'),(12764,3,148066,203764,'jungle demon'),(12765,3,351,4025,'go away'),(12766,3,2075,3373,'get hence quickly or the priest will turn thee into a wolf again'),(12767,3,108123,108123,'shoot buldeo shoot'),(12768,3,51,19767,'the old tower musket went off with a bang and a young buffalo bellowed in pain'),(12769,3,77,223922,'more sorcery'),(12770,3,142149,202737,'shouted the villagers'),(12771,3,258,183571,'he can turn bullets'),(12772,3,220532,136071,'buldeo that was thy buffalo'),(12773,3,2530,37,'now what is this'),(12774,3,2257,136568,'said mowgli bewildered as the stones flew thicker'),(12775,3,1056,35889,'they are not unlike the pack these brothers of thine said akela sitting down composedly'),(12776,3,67,976,'it is in my head that if bullets mean anything they would cast thee out'),(12777,3,203327,203294,'wolfs cub'),(12778,3,351,4025,'go away'),(12779,3,142149,136161,'shouted the priest waving a sprig of the sacred tulsi plant'),(12780,3,4196,1278,'last time it was because i was a man'),(12781,3,37,202228,'this time it is because i am a wolf'),(12782,3,2792,204273,'let us go akela'),(12783,3,23,1423,'a woman--it was messua--ran across to the herd and cried oh my son my son'),(12784,3,1056,865,'they say thou art a sorcerer who can turn himself into a beast at will'),(12785,3,279,203807,'i do not believe but go away or they will kill thee'),(12786,3,220532,511,'buldeo says thou art a wizard but i know thou hast avenged nathoos death'),(12787,3,3479,219377,'come back messua'),(12788,3,142149,41478,'shouted the crowd'),(12789,3,3479,203807,'come back or we will stone thee'),(12790,3,204077,2725,'mowgli laughed a little short ugly laugh for a stone had hit him in the mouth'),(12791,3,17034,219377,'run back messua'),(12792,3,37,194337,'this is one of the foolish tales they tell under the big tree at dusk'),(12793,3,279,534,'i have at least paid for thy sons life'),(12794,3,50041,224445,'farewell and run quickly for i shall send the herd in more swiftly than their brickbats'),(12795,3,279,219377,'i am no wizard messua'),(12796,3,2530,4916,'now once more akela he cried'),(12797,3,6853,50,'bring the herd in'),(12798,3,51,7711,'the buffaloes were anxious enough to get to the village'),(12799,3,1056,1811,'they hardly needed akelas yell but charged through the gate like a whirlwind scattering the crowd right and left'),(12800,3,5854,1134,'keep count'),(12801,3,142149,224494,'shouted mowgli scornfully'),(12802,3,67,112,'it may be that i have stolen one of them'),(12803,3,5854,77,'keep count for i will do your herding no more'),(12804,3,95828,26198,'fare you well children of men and thank messua that i do not come in with my wolves and hunt you up and down your street'),(12805,3,258,8220,'he turned on his heel and walked away with the lone wolf and as he looked up at the stars he felt happy'),(12806,3,655,204273,'no more sleeping in traps for me akela'),(12807,3,2792,4025,'let us get shere khans skin and go away'),(12808,3,655,424,'no we will not hurt the village for messua was kind to me'),(12809,3,483,2140,'when the moon rose over the plain making it look all milky the horrified villagers saw mowgli with two wolves at his heels and a bundle on his head trotting across at the steady wolfs trot that eats up the long miles like fire'),(12810,3,1502,784,'then they banged the temple bells and blew the conches louder than ever'),(12811,3,1,1278,'and messua cried and buldeo embroidered the story of his adventures in the jungle till he ended by saying that akela stood up on his hind legs and talked like a man'),(12812,3,51,157427,'the moon was just going down when mowgli and the two wolves came to the hill of the council rock and they stopped at mother wolfs cave'),(12813,3,1056,1426,'they have cast me out from the man-pack mother shouted mowgli but i come with the hide of shere khan to keep my word'),(12814,3,5751,127226,'mother wolf walked stiffly from the cave with the cubs behind her and her eyes glowed as she saw the skin'),(12815,3,279,176810,'i told him on that day when he crammed his head and shoulders into this cave hunting for thy life little frog--i told him that