'),(14119,3,1649,159623,'we sat down--a hundred of us the camel went on in a big square and the men piled our packs and saddles outside the square and they fired over our backs the men did on all sides of the square'),(14120,3,994,46,'what sort of men'),(14121,3,345,12535,'any men that came along'),(14122,3,2257,247329,'said the troop-horse'),(14123,3,1056,163,'they teach us in riding school to lie down and let our masters fire across us but dick cunliffe is the only man id trust to do that'),(14124,3,67,40255,'it tickles my girths and besides i cant see with my head on the ground'),(14125,3,994,2074,'what does it matter who fires across you'),(14126,3,2257,242843,'said the camel'),(14127,3,74,187973,'there are plenty of men and plenty of other camels close by and a great many clouds of smoke'),(14128,3,279,1502,'i am not frightened then'),(14129,3,279,18092,'i sit still and wait'),(14130,3,1,9700,'and yet said billy you dream bad dreams and upset the camp at night'),(14131,3,43,43,'well well'),(14132,3,509,409,'before id lie down not to speak of sitting down and let a man fire across me my heels and his head would have something to say to each other'),(14133,3,991,163,'did you ever hear anything so awful as that'),(14134,3,74,330,'there was a long silence and then one of the gun bullocks lifted up his big head and said this is very foolish indeed'),(14135,3,74,94122,'there is only one way of fighting'),(14136,3,5037,247646,'oh go on said billy'),(14137,3,8565,424,'please dont mind me'),(14138,3,279,164978,'i suppose you fellows fight standing on your tails'),(14139,3,241,10658,'only one way said the two together'),(14140,3,1056,249264,'they must have been twins'),(14141,3,37,608,'this is that way'),(14142,3,40,249285,'to put all twenty yoke of us to the big gun as soon as two tails trumpets'),(14143,3,1024,176368,'two tails is camp slang for the elephant'),(14144,3,994,284,'what does two tails trumpet for'),(14145,3,2257,247024,'said the young mule'),(14146,3,40,1473,'to show that he is not going any nearer to the smoke on the other side'),(14147,3,1024,249325,'two tails is a great coward'),(14148,3,1502,249333,'then we tug the big gun all together--heya--hullah'),(14149,3,1649,222280,'we do not climb like cats nor run like calves'),(14150,3,1649,8866,'we go across the level plain twenty yoke of us till we are unyoked again and we graze while the big guns talk across the plain to some town with mud walls and pieces of the wall fall out and the dust goes up as though many cattle were coming home'),(14151,3,1,170360,'and you choose that time for grazing'),(14152,3,2257,247024,'said the young mule'),(14153,3,163,409,'that time or any other'),(14154,3,36839,676,'eating is always good'),(14155,3,1649,67,'we eat till we are yoked up again and tug the gun back to where two tails is waiting for it'),(14156,3,841,1811,'sometimes there are big guns in the city that speak back and some of us are killed and then there is all the more grazing for those that are left'),(14157,3,37,76246,'this is fate'),(14158,3,2076,249325,'none the less two tails is a great coward'),(14159,3,163,93834,'that is the proper way to fight'),(14160,3,1649,249489,'we are brothers from hapur'),(14161,3,2043,246432,'our father was a sacred bull of shiva'),(14162,3,1649,15887,'we have spoken'),(14163,3,43,247329,'well ive certainly learned something tonight said the troop-horse'),(14164,3,513,2074,'do you gentlemen of the screw-gun battery feel inclined to eat when you are being fired at with big guns and two tails is behind you'),(14165,3,482,163858,'about as much as we feel inclined to sit down and let men sprawl all over us or run into people with knives'),(14166,3,279,131491,'i never heard such stuff'),(14167,3,23,247024,'a mountain ledge a well-balanced load a driver you can trust to let you pick your own way and im your mule'),(14168,3,249586,249588,'but--the other things--no'),(14169,3,2257,104164,'said billy with a stamp of his foot'),(14170,3,53,314,'of course said the troop horse everyone is not made in the same way and i can quite see that your family on your fathers side would fail to understand a great many things'),(14171,3,2027,220367,'never you mind my family on my fathers side said billy angrily for every mule hates to be reminded that his father was a donkey'),(14172,3,413,26307,'my father was a southern gentleman and he could pull down and bite and kick into rags every horse he came across'),(14173,3,1830,249683,'remember that you big brown brumby'),(14174,3,249683,8229,'brumby means wild horse without any breeding'),(14175,3,6766,102,'imagine the feelings of sunol if a car-horse called her a skate and you can imagine how the australian horse felt'),(14176,3,279,10482,'i saw the white of his eye glitter in the dark'),(14177,3,4334,130400,'see here you son of an imported malaga jackass he said between his teeth id have you know that im related on my mothers side to carbine winner of the melbourne cup and where i come from we arent accustomed to being ridden over roughshod by any parrot-mouthed pig-headed mule in a pop-gun pea-shooter battery'),(14178,3,60,12987,'are you ready'),(14179,3,407,133223,'on your hind legs'),(14180,3,242734,247646,'squealed billy'),(14181,3,1056,74,'they both reared up facing each other and i was expecting a furious fight when a gurgly rumbly voice called out of the darkness to the right--children what are you fighting about there'),(14182,3,104,53992,'be quiet'),(14183,3,1191,4517,'both beasts dropped down with a snort of disgust for neither horse nor mule can bear to listen to an elephants voice'),(14184,3,153,164978,'its two tails'),(14185,3,2257,247329,'said the troop-horse'),(14186,3,279,247,'i cant stand him'),(14187,3,23,24172,'a tail at each end isnt fair'),(14188,3,413,1028,'my feelings exactly said billy crowding into the troop-horse for company'),(14189,3,798,314,'were very alike in some things'),(14190,3,279,4355,'i suppose weve inherited them from our mothers said the 