 spreading out into a line'),(14368,3,163,159396,'that line grew and grew and grew till it was three-quarters of a mile long from wing to wing--one solid wall of men horses and guns'),(14369,3,1502,18376,'then it came on straight toward the viceroy and the amir and as it got nearer the ground began to shake like the deck of a steamer when the engines are going fast'),(14370,3,2647,51283,'unless you have been there you cannot imagine what a frightening effect this steady come-down of troops has on the spectators even when they know it is only a review'),(14371,3,279,246661,'i looked at the amir'),(14372,3,1274,2224,'up till then he had not shown the shadow of a sign of astonishment or anything else'),(14373,3,295,247,'but now his eyes began to get bigger and bigger and he picked up the reins on his horses neck and looked behind him'),(14374,3,284,1886,'for a minute it seemed as though he were going to draw his sword and slash his way out through the english men and women in the carriages at the back'),(14375,3,1502,10658,'then the advance stopped dead the ground stood still the whole line saluted and thirty bands began to play all together'),(14376,3,163,252130,'that was the end of the review and the regiments went off to their camps in the rain and an infantry band struck up with-- the animals went in two by two hurrah'),(14377,3,51,13415,'the animals went in two by two the elephant and the battery mul and they all got into the ark for to get out of the rain'),(14378,3,1502,26251,'then i heard an old grizzled long-haired central asian chief who had come down with the amir asking questions of a native officer'),(14379,3,2530,3873,'now said he in what manner was this wonderful thing done'),(14380,3,1,65795,'and the officer answered an order was given and they obeyed'),(14381,3,295,46,'but are the beasts as wise as the men'),(14382,3,2257,3650,'said the chief'),(14383,3,1056,513,'they obey as the men do'),(14384,3,247024,252278,'mule horse elephant or bullock he obeys 