alked'),(15487,4,5543,2011,'since so many rooms had been built people must have lived in them but it all seemed so empty that she could not quite believe it true'),(15488,4,67,4543,'it was not until she climbed to the second floor that she thought of turning the handle of a door'),(15489,4,172,273,'all the doors were shut as mrs'),(15490,4,255890,67,'medlock had said they were but at last she put her hand on the handle of one of them and turned it'),(15491,4,729,12842,'she was almost frightened for a moment when she felt that it turned without difficulty and that when she pushed upon the door itself it slowly and heavily opened'),(15492,4,67,236653,'it was a massive door and opened into a big bedroom'),(15493,4,74,6317,'there were embroidered hangings on the wall and inlaid furniture such as she had seen in india stood about the room'),(15494,4,23,784,'a broad window with leaded panes looked out upon the moor and over the mantel was another portrait of the stiff plain little girl who seemed to stare at her more curiously than ever'),(15495,4,290,245,'perhaps she slept here once said mary'),(15496,4,729,130109,'she stares at me so that she makes me feel queer'),(15497,4,171,77,'after that she opened more doors and more'),(15498,4,729,112,'she saw so many rooms that she became quite tired and began to think that there must be a hundred though she had not counted them'),(15499,4,50,112,'in all of them there were old pictures or old tapestries with strange scenes worked on them'),(15500,4,74,112,'there were curious pieces of furniture and curious ornaments in nearly all of them'),(15501,4,50,136182,'in one room which looked like a lady\'s sitting-room the hangings were all embroidered velvet and in a cabinet were about a hundred little elephants made of ivory'),(15502,4,1056,160378,'they were of different sizes and some had their mahouts or palanquins on their backs'),(15503,4,144,135552,'some were much bigger than the others and some were so tiny that they seemed only 