ook at me'),(16305,4,279,139136,'i wants a bit of a chat'),(16306,4,74,168659,'there he is in the bush'),(16307,4,3326,258,'whose is he'),(16308,4,129787,245,'he\'s ben weatherstaff\'s but i think he knows me a little answered mary'),(16309,4,257803,3373,'aye he knows thee said dickon in his low voice again'),(16310,4,144004,203807,'an\' he likes thee'),(16311,4,129787,407,'he\'s took thee on'),(16312,4,272813,26616,'he\'ll tell me all about thee in a minute'),(16313,4,258,265032,'he moved quite close to the bush with the slow movement mary had noticed before and then he made a sound almost like the robin\'s own twitter'),(16314,4,51,9590,'the robin listened a few seconds intently and then answered quite as if he were replying to a question'),(16315,4,257803,252835,'aye he\'s a friend o\' yours chuckled dickon'),(16316,4,513,75,'do you think he is'),(16317,4,4916,11618,'cried mary eagerly'),(16318,4,729,515,'she did so want to know'),(16319,4,513,424,'do you think he really likes me'),(16320,4,258,252835,'he wouldn\'t come near thee if he didn\'t answered dickon'),(16321,4,103882,1278,'birds is rare choosers an\' a robin can flout a body worse than a man'),(16322,4,4334,2530,'see he\'s making up to thee now'),(16323,4,279519,139468,'\'cannot tha\' see a chap'),(16324,4,129787,181535,'he\'s sayin\''),(16325,4,1,2011,'and it really seemed as if it must be true'),(16326,4,258,168659,'he so sidled and twittered and tilted as he hopped on his bush'),(16327,4,513,794,'do you understand everything birds say'),(16328,4,2257,245,'said mary'),(16329,4,260877,1999,'dickon\'s grin spread until he seemed all wide red curving mouth and he rubbed his rough head'),(16330,4,279,2257,'i think i do and they think i do he said'),(16331,4,127793,2583,'i\'ve lived on th\' moor with \'em so long'),(16332,4,127793,179730,'i\'ve watched \'em break shell an\' come out an\' fledge an\' learn to fly an\' begin to sing till i think i\'m one of \'em'),(16333,4,841,67,'sometimes i think p\'raps i