d three hundred yards of wincey to the asylum'),(20710,5,144,2074,'some people said it was because he couldnt sell it but id rather believe that it was out of the kindness of his heart wouldnt you'),(20711,5,483,424,'when we got on the train i felt as if everybody must be looking at me and pitying me'),(20712,5,295,156593,'but i just went to work and imagined that i had on the most beautiful pale blue silk dress--because when you are imagining you might as well imagine something worth while--and a big hat all flowers and nodding plumes and a gold watch and kid gloves and boots'),(20713,5,279,251,'i felt cheered up right away and i enjoyed my trip to the island with all my might'),(20714,5,279,137175,'i wasnt a bit sick coming over in the boat'),(20715,5,3483,273,'neither was mrs'),(20716,5,335273,75,'spencer although she generally is'),(20717,5,729,338228,'she said she hadnt time to get sick watching to see that i didnt fall overboard'),(20718,5,729,482,'she said she never saw the beat of me for prowling about'),(20719,5,295,67,'but if it kept her from being seasick its a mercy i did prowl isnt it'),(20720,5,1,10463,'and i wanted to see everything that was to be seen on that boat because i didnt know whether id ever have another opportunity'),(20721,5,5037,190939,'oh there are a lot more cherry-trees all in bloom'),(20722,5,37,461,'this island is the bloomiest place'),(20723,5,279,454,'i just love it already and im so glad im going to live here'),(20724,5,226572,126,'ive always heard that prince edward island was the prettiest place in the world and i used to imagine i was living here but i never really expected i would'),(20725,5,153,67,'its delightful when your imaginations come true isnt it'),(20726,5,295,140418,'but those red roads are so funny'),(20727,5,483,273,'when we got into the train at charlottetown and the red roads began to flash past i asked mrs'),(20728,5,335273,6503,'spencer what made them red and she said she didnt know and for pitys sake not to as