ely place to live--in an apple blossom'),(21899,5,8104,67,'fancy going to sleep in it when the wind was rocking it'),(21900,5,257,192033,'if i wasnt a human girl i think id like to be a bee and live among the flowers'),(21901,5,13685,333265,'yesterday you wanted to be a sea-gull sniffed marilla'),(21902,5,279,134413,'i think you are very fickle minded'),(21903,5,279,5107,'i told you to learn that prayer and not talk'),(21904,5,295,2074,'but it seems impossible for you to stop talking if youve got anybody that will listen to you'),(21905,5,1051,67,'so go up to your room and learn it'),(21906,5,5037,3217,'oh i know it pretty nearly all now--all but just the last line'),(21907,5,43,2074,'well never mind do as i tell you'),(21908,5,351,20644,'go to your room and finish learning it well and stay there until i call you down to help me get tea'),(21909,5,850,1028,'can i take the apple blossoms with me for company'),(21910,5,47825,30104,'pleaded anne'),(21911,5,655,192033,'no you dont want your room cluttered up with flowers'),(21912,5,2074,461,'you should have left them on the tree in the first place'),(21913,5,279,30104,'i did feel a little that way too said anne'),(21914,5,279,345286,'i kind of felt i shouldnt shorten their lovely lives by picking them--i wouldnt want to be picked if i were an apple blossom'),(21915,5,295,161730,'but the temptation was irresistible'),(21916,5,994,32849,'what do you do when you meet with an irresistible temptation'),(21917,5,30104,6317,'anne did you hear me tell you to go to your room'),(21918,5,30104,6694,'anne sighed retreated to the east gable and sat down in a chair by the window'),(21919,5,124163,228480,'there--i know this prayer'),(21920,5,279,24669,'i learned that last sentence coming upstairs'),(21921,5,2530,41380,'now im going to imagine things into this room so that theyll always stay imagined'),(21922,5,51,26928,'the floor is covered with a white velvet carpet with pink roses all over it and there are pink silk curtains at the 