ess youre all right at anything'),(23824,5,368456,18262,'phillips told me last week in blairs store at carmody that you was the smartest scholar in school and was making rapid progress'),(23825,5,12450,2458,'rapid progress was his very words'),(23826,5,226864,106,'theres them as runs down teddy phillips and says he aint much of a teacher but i guess hes all right'),(23827,5,333259,106,'matthew would have thought anyone who praised anne was all right'),(23828,5,4348,30104,'im sure id get on better with geometry if only he wouldnt change the letters complained anne'),(23829,5,279,1274,'i learn the proposition off by heart and then he draws it on the blackboard and puts different letters from what are in the book and i get all mixed up'),(23830,5,279,2074,'i dont think a teacher should take such a mean advantage do you'),(23831,5,798,13125,'were studying agriculture now and ive found out at last what makes the roads red'),(23832,5,153,13768,'its a great comfort'),(23833,5,279,273,'i wonder how marilla and mrs'),(23834,5,333254,2601,'lynde are enjoying themselves'),(23835,5,333254,379073,'lynde says canada is going to the dogs the way things are being run at ottawa and that its an awful warning to the electors'),(23836,5,729,3441,'she says if women were allowed to vote we would soon see a blessed change'),(23837,5,994,333259,'what way do you vote matthew'),(23838,5,379095,316304,'conservative said matthew promptly'),(23839,5,40,379106,'to vote conservative was part of matthews religion'),(23840,5,1502,16413,'then im conservative too said anne decidedly'),(23841,5,4348,379125,'im glad because gil--because some of the boys in school are grits'),(23842,5,279,636,'i guess mr'),(23843,5,368456,378556,'phillips is a grit too because prissy andrewss father is one and ruby gillis says that when a man is courting he always has to agree with the girls mother in religion and her father in politics'),(23844,5,75,333259,'is that true matthew'),(23845,5,43,333259,'well now i dunno said matthew'),(23846,5,991,333259,'did you ever go courting matthew'),(23847,5,43,30136,'well now no i dunnos i ever did said matthew who had certainly never thought of such a thing in his whole existence'),(23848,5,30104,22498,'anne reflected with her chin in her hands'),(23849,5,67,333259,'it must be rather interesting dont you think matthew'),(23850,5,332585,76325,'ruby gillis says when she grows up shes going to have ever so many beaus on the string and have them all crazy about her but i think that would be too exciting'),(23851,5,130931,2129,'id rather have just one in his right mind'),(23852,5,295,273,'but ruby gillis knows a great deal about such matters because she has so many big sisters and mrs'),(23853,5,333254,374258,'lynde says the gillis girls have gone off like hot cakes'),(23854,5,368456,5695,'phillips goes up to see prissy andrews nearly every evening'),(23855,5,258,172,'he says it is to help her with her lessons but miranda sloane is studying for queens too and i should think she needed help a lot more than prissy because shes ever so much stupider but he never goes to help her in the evenings at all'),(23856,5,74,333259,'there are a great many things in this world that i cant understand very well matthew'),(23857,5,43,333259,'well now i dunno as i comprehend them all myself acknowledged matthew'),(23858,5,43,205888,'well i suppose i must finish up my lessons'),(23859,5,279,2751,'i wont allow myself to open that new book jane lent me until im through'),(23860,5,295,333259,'but its a terrible temptation matthew'),(23861,5,1232,11635,'even when i turn my back on it i can see it there just as plain'),(23862,5,4,67,'jane said she cried herself sick over it'),(23863,5,279,98162,'i love a book that makes me cry'),(23864,5,295,252814,'but i think ill carry that book into the sitting room and lock it in the jam closet and give you the key'),(23865,5,1,90159,'and you must not give it to me matthew until my lessons are done not even if i implore you on my be