citations and everybody has to say a piece or take part in a dialogue'),(24994,5,5037,67,'oh its just glorious to think of it'),(24995,5,369126,12447,'josie pye says she hates it but that is just because josie has so little imagination'),(24996,5,4247,31813,'diana and ruby gillis and jane andrews are preparing a dialogue called a morning visit for next friday'),(24997,5,1,103882,'and the friday afternoons they dont have recitations miss stacy takes them all to the woods for a field day and they study ferns and flowers and birds'),(24998,5,1,5695,'and they have physical culture exercises every morning and evening'),(24999,5,333254,204817,'lynde says she never heard of such goings on and it all comes of having a lady teacher'),(25000,5,295,2667,'but i think it must be splendid and i believe i shall find that miss stacy is a kindred spirit'),(25001,5,226864,172,'theres one thing plain to be seen anne said marilla and that is that your fall off the barry roof hasnt injured your tongue at all'),(25002,5,4328,4521,'chapter xxiv'),(25003,5,334,395597,'miss stacy and her pupils get up a concert it was october again when anne was ready to go back to school--a glorious october all red and gold with mellow mornings when the valleys were filled with delicate mists as if the spirit of autumn had poured them in for the sun to drain--amethyst pearl silver rose and smoke-blue'),(25004,5,51,2751,'the dews were so heavy that the fields glistened like cloth of silver and there were such heaps of rustling leaves in the hollows of many-stemmed woods to run crisply through'),(25005,5,51,67,'the birch path was a canopy of yellow and the ferns were sear and brown all along it'),(25006,5,74,55103,'there was a tang in the very air that inspired the hearts of small maidens tripping unlike snails swiftly and willingly to school and it was jolly to be back again at the little brown desk beside diana with ruby gillis nodding across the aisle and carrie sloane sending up notes and julia bell passing a chew of gum down from the back seat'),(25007,5,30104,130797,'anne drew a long breath of happiness as she sharpened her pencil and arranged her picture cards in her desk'),(25008,5,534,2323,'life was certainly very interesting'),(25009,5,50,1343,'in the new teacher she found another true and helpful friend'),(25010,5,334,395779,'miss stacy was a bright sympathetic young woman with the happy gift of winning and holding the affections of her pupils and bringing out the best that was in them mentally and morally'),(25011,5,30104,395805,'anne expanded like a flower under this wholesome influence and carried home to the admiring matthew and the critical marilla glowing accounts of schoolwork and aims'),(25012,5,279,333265,'i love miss stacy with my whole heart marilla'),(25013,5,729,4517,'she is so ladylike and she has such a sweet voice'),(25014,5,483,197070,'when she pronounces my name i feel instinctively that shes spelling it with an e'),(25015,5,1649,73952,'we had recitations this afternoon'),(25016,5,279,395861,'i just wish you could have been there to hear me recite mary queen of scots'),(25017,5,279,67,'i just put my whole soul into it'),(25018,5,332585,1905,'ruby gillis told me coming home that the way i said the line now for my fathers arm she said my womans heart farewell just made her blood run cold'),(25019,5,43,333259,'well now you might recite it for me some of these days out in the barn suggested matthew'),(25020,5,53,515,'of course i will said anne meditatively but i wont be able to do it so well i know'),(25021,5,67,2458,'it wont be so exciting as it is when you have a whole schoolful before you hanging breathlessly on your words'),(25022,5,279,1905,'i know i wont be able to make your blood run cold'),(25023,5,333254,333265,'lynde says it made her blood run cold to see the boys climbing to the very tops of those big trees on bells hill after crows nests last friday said marilla'),(25024,5,279,67,'i wonder at miss stacy for encouraging it'),(25025,5