one of not telling us the truth unless we have proof that theyre not'),(25623,5,279,1833,'i have proof now--green hair is proof enough for anybody'),(25624,5,295,404512,'but i hadnt then and i believed every word he said implicitly'),(25625,5,59,2257,'who said'),(25626,5,59,482,'who are you talking about'),(25627,5,51,73952,'the peddler that was here this afternoon'),(25628,5,279,247,'i bought the dye from him'),(25629,5,30104,1889,'anne shirley how often have i told you never to let one of those italians in the house'),(25630,5,279,172,'i dont believe in encouraging them to come around at all'),(25631,5,5037,1889,'oh i didnt let him in the house'),(25632,5,279,6583,'i remembered what you told me and i went out carefully shut the door and looked at his things on the step'),(25633,5,16049,404600,'besides he wasnt an italian--he was a german jew'),(25634,5,258,196882,'he had a big box full of very interesting things and he told me he was working hard to make enough money to bring his wife and children out from germany'),(25635,5,258,1308,'he spoke so feelingly about them that it touched my heart'),(25636,5,279,9198,'i wanted to buy something from him to help him in such a worthy object'),(25637,5,1502,404392,'then all at once i saw the bottle of hair dye'),(25638,5,51,891,'the peddler said it was warranted to dye any hair a beautiful raven black and wouldnt wash off'),(25639,5,50,161730,'in a trice i saw myself with beautiful raven-black hair and the temptation was irresistible'),(25640,5,295,29521,'but the price of the bottle was seventy-five cents and i had only fifty cents left out of my chicken money'),(25641,5,279,4025,'i think the peddler had a very kind heart for he said that seeing it was me hed sell it for fifty cents and that was just giving it away'),(25642,5,1051,2257,'so i bought it and as soon as he had gone i came up here and applied it with an old hairbrush as the directions said'),(25643,5,279,2074,'i used up the whole bottle and oh marilla when i saw