 was any'),(25666,5,1373,608,'your hair must be cut off there is no other way'),(25667,5,2074,163,'you cant go out with it looking like that'),(25668,5,59486,18163,'annes lips quivered but she realized the bitter truth of marillas remarks'),(25669,5,34,376830,'with a dismal sigh she went for the scissors'),(25670,5,8565,554,'please cut it off at once marilla and have it over'),(25671,5,5037,44639,'oh i feel that my heart is broken'),(25672,5,37,96843,'this is such an unromantic affliction'),(25673,5,51,76,'the girls in books lose their hair in fevers or sell it to get money for some good deed and im sure i wouldnt mind losing my hair in some such fashion half so much'),(25674,5,295,74,'but there is nothing comforting in having your hair cut off because youve dyed it a dreadful color is there'),(25675,5,4348,21272,'im going to weep all the time youre cutting it off if it wont interfere'),(25676,5,67,109,'it seems such a tragic thing'),(25677,5,30104,41483,'anne wept then but later on when she went upstairs and looked in the glass she was calm with despair'),(25678,5,333265,346,'marilla had done her work thoroughly and it had been necessary to shingle the hair as closely as possible'),(25679,5,51,104,'the result was not becoming to state the case as mildly as may be'),(25680,5,30104,132350,'anne promptly turned her glass to the wall'),(25681,5,5886,280030,'ill never never look at myself again until my hair grows she exclaimed passionately'),(25682,5,1502,90259,'then she suddenly righted the glass'),(25683,5,9487,813,'yes i will too'),(25684,5,130931,608,'id do penance for being wicked that way'),(25685,5,5886,1711,'ill look at myself every time i come to my room and see how ugly i am'),(25686,5,1,3279,'and i wont try to imagine it away either'),(25687,5,279,230635,'i never thought i was vain about my hair of all things but now i know i was in spite of its being red because it was so long and thick and curly'),(25688,5,279,5026,'i expect something will happen to my nos