 of gold for coverlet there was none but an old piano scarf of yellow japanese crepe was an excellent substitute'),(25768,5,23,12385,'a white lily was not obtainable just then but the effect of a tall blue iris placed in one of annes folded hands was all that could be desired'),(25769,5,2530,4,'now shes all ready said jane'),(25770,5,1649,850,'we must kiss her quiet brows and diana you say sister farewell forever and ruby you say farewell sweet sister both of you as sorrowfully as you possibly can'),(25771,5,30104,262,'anne for goodness sake smile a little'),(25772,5,2074,9164,'you know elaine lay as though she smiled'),(25773,5,228305,949,'thats better'),(25774,5,2530,891,'now push the flat off'),(25775,5,51,21058,'the flat was accordingly pushed off scraping roughly over an old embedded stake in the process'),(25776,5,4247,43146,'diana and jane and ruby only waited long enough to see it caught in the current and headed for the bridge before scampering up through the woods across the road and down to the lower headland where as lancelot and guinevere and the king they were to be in readiness to receive the lily maid'),(25777,5,284,1844,'for a few minutes anne drifting slowly down enjoyed the romance of her situation to the full'),(25778,5,1502,234,'then something happened not at all romantic'),(25779,5,51,200556,'the flat began to leak'),(25780,5,50,111442,'in a very few moments it was necessary for elaine to scramble to her feet pick up her cloth of gold coverlet and pall of blackest samite and gaze blankly at a big crack in the bottom of her barge through which the water was literally pouring'),(25781,5,163,19095,'that sharp stake at the landing had torn off the strip of batting nailed on the flat'),(25782,5,30104,406874,'anne did not know this but it did not take her long to realize that she was in a dangerous plight'),(25783,5,308,406002,'at this rate the flat would fill and sink long before it could drift to the lower headland'),(25784,5,4187,165296,'where were the oars'),(25785,5,1811,147260,'left behind at the landing'),(25786,5,30104,406924,'anne gave one gasping little scream which nobody ever heard she was white to the lips but she did not lose her self-possession'),(25787,5,74,139,'there was one chance--just one'),(25788,5,279,273,'i was horribly frightened she told mrs'),(25789,5,389358,2845,'allan the next day and it seemed like years while the flat was drifting down to the bridge and the water rising in it every moment'),(25790,5,279,273,'i prayed mrs'),(25791,5,389358,67,'allan most earnestly but i didnt shut my eyes to pray for i knew the only way god could save me was to let the flat float close enough to one of the bridge piles for me to climb up on it'),(25792,5,2074,112,'you know the piles are just old tree trunks and there are lots of knots and old branch stubs on them'),(25793,5,67,67,'it was proper to pray but i had to do my part by watching out and right well i knew it'),(25794,5,279,3373,'i just said dear god please take the flat close to a pile and ill do the rest over and over again'),(25795,5,3470,228480,'under such circumstances you dont think much about making a flowery prayer'),(25796,5,295,191490,'but mine was answered for the flat bumped right into a pile for a minute and i flung the scarf and the shawl over my shoulder and scrambled up on a big providential stub'),(25797,5,1,273,'and there i was mrs'),(25798,5,389358,4332,'allan clinging to that slippery old pile with no way of getting up or down'),(25799,5,67,369,'it was a very unromantic position but i didnt think about that at the time'),(25800,5,2074,12132,'you dont think much about romance when you have just escaped from a watery grave'),(25801,5,279,118264,'i said a grateful prayer at once and then i gave all my attention to holding on tight for i knew i should probably have to depend on human aid to get back to dry land'),(25802,5,51,407215,'the flat drifted under the bridge and then promptly sank in midstream'),(25803,5,332585,67,'rub