ays as simply as possible'),(26473,5,67,183,'it was hard at first'),(26474,5,279,112,'i was so used to crowding in all the fine big words i could think of--and i thought of any number of them'),(26475,5,295,949,'but ive got used to it now and i see its so much better'),(26476,5,994,129857,'what has become of your story club'),(26477,5,279,369,'i havent heard you speak of it for a long time'),(26478,5,51,16111,'the story club isnt in existence any longer'),(26479,5,1649,67,'we hadnt time for it--and anyhow i think we had got tired of it'),(26480,5,67,140283,'it was silly to be writing about love and murder and elopements and mysteries'),(26481,5,334,813,'miss stacy sometimes has us write a story for training in composition but she wont let us write anything but what might happen in avonlea in our own lives and she criticizes it very sharply and makes us criticize our own too'),(26482,5,279,1718,'i never thought my compositions had so many faults until i began to look for them myself'),(26483,5,279,137243,'i felt so ashamed i wanted to give up altogether but miss stacy said i could learn to write well if i only trained myself to be my own severest critic'),(26484,5,1,40,'and so i am trying to'),(26485,5,226481,333265,'youve only two more months before the entrance said marilla'),(26486,5,513,2751,'do you think youll be able to get through'),(26487,5,30104,244700,'anne shivered'),(26488,5,279,515,'i dont know'),(26489,5,841,6416,'sometimes i think ill be all right--and then i get horribly afraid'),(26490,5,218723,163,'weve studied hard and miss stacy has drilled us thoroughly but we maynt get through for all that'),(26491,5,218723,175096,'weve each got a stumbling block'),(26492,5,9989,371148,'mine is geometry of course and janes is latin and ruby and charlies is algebra and josies is arithmetic'),(26493,5,400907,1693,'moody spurgeon says he feels it in his bones that he is going to fail in english history'),(26494,5,334,3968,'miss stacy is going to give us examination