369126,26304,'josie just scraped through with three marks to spare but youll see shell put on as many airs as if shed led'),(26639,5,122422,4453,'wont miss stacy be delighted'),(26640,5,5037,163,'oh anne what does it feel like to see your name at the head of a pass list like that'),(26641,5,257,6219,'if it were me i know id go crazy with joy'),(26642,5,279,5695,'i am pretty near crazy as it is but youre as calm and cool as a spring evening'),(26643,5,4348,30104,'im just dazzled inside said anne'),(26644,5,279,50,'i want to say a hundred things and i cant find words to say them in'),(26645,5,279,855,'i never dreamed of this--yes i did too just once'),(26646,5,279,183,'i let myself think once what if i should come out first'),(26647,5,420708,225856,'quakingly you know for it seemed so vain and presumptuous to think i could lead the island'),(26648,5,9933,4247,'excuse me a minute diana'),(26649,5,279,333259,'i must run right out to the field to tell matthew'),(26650,5,1502,90,'then well go up the road and tell the good news to the others'),(26651,5,1056,273,'they hurried to the hayfield below the barn where matthew was coiling hay and as luck would have it mrs'),(26652,5,333254,369186,'lynde was talking to marilla at the lane fence'),(26653,5,5037,183,'oh matthew exclaimed anne ive passed and im first--or one of the first'),(26654,5,4348,19569,'im not vain but im thankful'),(26655,5,43,282964,'well now i always said it said matthew gazing at the pass list delightedly'),(26656,5,279,2944,'i knew you could beat them all easy'),(26657,5,226481,273,'youve done pretty well i must say anne said marilla trying to hide her extreme pride in anne from mrs'),(26658,5,333856,902,'rachels critical eye'),(26659,5,295,67,'but that good soul said heartily i just guess she has done well and far be it from me to be backward in saying it'),(26660,5,218673,2074,'youre a credit to your friends anne thats what and were all proud of you'),(26661,5,163,273,'that night anne who had wound up the delightful evening with a serious little talk with mrs'),(26662,5,389358,1308,'allan at the manse knelt sweetly by her open window in a great sheen of moonshine and murmured a prayer of gratitude and aspiration that came straight from her heart'),(26663,5,74,5370,'there was in it thankfulness for the past and reverent petition for the future and when she slept on her white pillow her dreams were as fair and bright and beautiful as maidenhood might desire'),(26664,5,4328,61117,'chapter xxxiii'),(26665,5,51,16413,'the hotel concert put on your white organdy by all means anne advised diana decidedly'),(26666,5,1056,135772,'they were together in the east gable chamber outside it was only twilight--a lovely yellowish-green twilight with a clear-blue cloudless sky'),(26667,5,23,21527,'a big round moon slowly deepening from her pallid luster into burnished silver hung over the haunted wood the air was full of sweet summer sounds--sleepy birds twittering freakish breezes faraway voices and laughter'),(26668,5,295,826,'but in annes room the blind was drawn and the lamp lighted for an important toilet was being made'),(26669,5,51,158468,'the east gable was a very different place from what it had been on that night four years before when anne had felt its bareness penetrate to the marrow of her spirit with its inhospitable chill'),(26670,5,109928,5370,'changes had crept in marilla conniving at them resignedly until it was as sweet and dainty a nest as a young girl could desire'),(26671,5,51,112,'the velvet carpet with the pink roses and the pink silk curtains of annes early visions had certainly never materialized but her dreams had kept pace with her growth and it is not probable she lamented them'),(26672,5,51,26217,'the floor was covered with a pretty matting and the curtains that softened the high window and fluttered in the vagrant breezes were of pale-green art muslin'),(26673,5,51,273,'the walls hung not with gold and silver brocade tapestry but with a dainty apple-bl