er under her wing and introduced her to everybody and everybody was very nice to her'),(26811,5,51,273,'the professional elocutionist mrs'),(26812,5,423611,213225,'evans came and chatted with her telling her that she had a charming voice and interpreted her selections beautifully'),(26813,5,1232,8273,'even the white-lace girl paid her a languid little compliment'),(26814,5,1056,4947,'they had supper in the big beautifully decorated dining room diana and jane were invited to partake of this also since they had come with anne but billy was nowhere to be found having decamped in mortal fear of some such invitation'),(26815,5,258,143452,'he was in waiting for them with the team however when it was all over and the three girls came merrily out into the calm white moonshine radiance'),(26816,5,30104,347462,'anne breathed deeply and looked into the clear sky beyond the dark boughs of the firs'),(26817,5,5037,9700,'oh it was good to be out again in the purity and silence of the night'),(26818,5,1338,423769,'how great and still and wonderful everything was with the murmur of the sea sounding through it and the darkling cliffs beyond like grim giants guarding enchanted coasts'),(26819,5,347717,369,'hasnt it been a perfectly splendid time'),(26820,5,91048,4025,'sighed jane as they drove away'),(26821,5,279,2045,'i just wish i was a rich american and could spend my summer at a hotel and wear jewels and low-necked dresses and have ice cream and chicken salad every blessed day'),(26822,5,4348,873,'im sure it would be ever so much more fun than teaching school'),(26823,5,30104,10508,'anne your recitation was simply great although i thought at first you were never going to begin'),(26824,5,279,273,'i think it was better than mrs'),(26825,5,5037,5426,'oh no dont say things like that jane said anne quickly because it sounds silly'),(26826,5,67,273,'it couldnt be better than mrs'),(26827,5,423873,365779,'evanss you know for she is a professional and im only a schoolgirl with a little 