st will be in town tomorrow and he insists that i must go in and have my eyes examined'),(27316,5,279,554,'i suppose id better go and have it over'),(27317,5,5886,917,'ill be more than thankful if the man can give me the right kind of glasses to suit my eyes'),(27318,5,2074,2074,'you wont mind staying here alone while im away will you'),(27319,5,277793,513,'martin will have to drive me in and theres ironing and baking to do'),(27320,5,279,106,'i shall be all right'),(27321,5,4247,424,'diana will come over for company for me'),(27322,5,279,391131,'i shall attend to the ironing and baking beautifully--you neednt fear that ill starch the handkerchiefs or flavor the cake with liniment'),(27323,5,333265,15178,'marilla laughed'),(27324,5,994,30104,'what a girl you were for making mistakes in them days anne'),(27325,5,2074,384582,'you were always getting into scrapes'),(27326,5,279,86966,'i did use to think you were possessed'),(27327,5,513,14884,'do you mind the time you dyed your hair'),(27328,5,9487,330,'yes indeed'),(27329,5,279,1999,'i shall never forget it smiled anne touching the heavy braid of hair that was wound about her shapely head'),(27330,5,279,1502,'i laugh a little now sometimes when i think what a worry my hair used to be to me--but i dont laugh much because it was a very real trouble then'),(27331,5,279,339152,'i did suffer terribly over my hair and my freckles'),(27332,5,413,369127,'my freckles are really gone and people are nice enough to tell me my hair is auburn now--all but josie pye'),(27333,5,729,67,'she informed me yesterday that she really thought it was redder than ever or at least my black dress made it look redder and she asked me if people who had red hair ever got used to having it'),(27334,5,333265,369127,'marilla ive almost decided to give up trying to like josie pye'),(27335,5,226572,706,'ive made what i would once have called a heroic effort to like her but josie pye wont be liked'),(27336,5,369126,3271,'josie is a pye said marilla sharp